```
Why we chose PostgreSQL over MongoDB for our SaaS product.

When you're building a property management platform, your data is
deeply relational:

→ Accounts have Properties
→ Properties have Units
→ Units have Tenants
→ Tenants have Rent Payments
→ Rent Payments have Transactions

Every entity connects to 3-4 others.

MongoDB would have forced us to either:
• Duplicate data everywhere (nightmare to maintain)
• Use $lookup for every query (slower than SQL JOINs)

With PostgreSQL + Prisma:
• One schema, fully typed
• JOINs are native and fast
• Prisma generates TypeScript types automatically
• Migrations are version-controlled

For relational SaaS data, PostgreSQL wins.
For unstructured/document data, MongoDB wins.

Choose based on your data shape, not hype.

#database #postgresql #mongodb #backend
```

