3 TypeScript tips from building 200+ APIs 🧵

1/ Use Zod for runtime validation.
TypeScript checks types at compile time.
Zod checks them at runtime.
Both together = bulletproof.

2/ Never use `any`.
Use `unknown` + type guards instead.
`any` defeats the purpose of TypeScript.

3/ Use discriminated unions for API responses.
type ApiResponse = 
  | { success: true; data: User }
  | { success: false; error: string }

#typescript #nodejs #webdev
```

